I am still not sure what you wish to do.  Do you want all autolinked assignments to have the same icon next to them? This should not be hard on the system level. You should be able to add something like 
```text
 .autolink {
  background: url('http://yoursite/yourimage.png');
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  padding-left: 30px
}
```
 to the theme somehow (Custom CSS in many theme settings). This should then add an image to the left of all the link. However, it sounds like you may be wanting to set a custom image manually for each link. I am not sure what the purpose of that would be. If you code hard links to something in the course instead of using a filter, the result will not be portable. The links will break if you move or copy the course.

This is turning out to be really a theme question rather than and editor problem.   There may already be some themes that do this.  Some of them do use different navagation techniques.  The theme forum might be more help. However if you only have the two icons for forward and back, you can do what you describe above simply with the CSS 
```text
.autolink {
  background: url('http://yoursite/forward.png');
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  padding-left: 30px;
  position: absolute;
  clip: rectangle(0px,30px,30px,0px);
  overflow: hidden
}
b, strong .autolink {
  background: url('http://yoursite/backward.png');
}
```
 The forward arrow will be displayed for plain assignment names. If the teacher places the text in bold, then the back arrow is displayed.

