Hello! After about 6 months running moodle without the HTML editor, today I finally used the mozilla javascript console to find out where was the bug. I just discovered my hosting provider was injecting HTML advertisement code right into the javascript code in /lib/editor/htmlarea/htmlarea.php The solution is easy: making some replacements in code in order to avoid "</head>" and "<body>" appear in javascript code. 1- Replace: HTMLArea.RE_head = /<head>((.|
)*?)</head>/i; HTMLArea.RE_body = /<body>((.|
)*?)</body>/i; With: HTMLArea.RE_head = /<h[e]ad>((.|
)*?)</h[e]ad>/i; HTMLArea.RE_body = /<b[o]dy>((.|
)*?)</b[o]dy>/i; 2- Replace: html += "</head>
"; html += '</body>
'; with: html += "</he"+"ad>
"; html += '</bo'+'dy>
'; 3- Replace: html += "</head>"; with: html +="</he"+"ad>"; This procedure specially applies for those using the same hosting provider I use, byethost. I will post this same solution into byethost help forums.

